<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/glossary#sarissa">Glossary</a> · Term · weapon</p><h1 class="enc-title">Sarissa</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The sarissa was a very long pike, several metres in length, carried by the infantry of the Macedonian <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/phalanx">phalanx</a>. Introduced under Philip II, it allowed several ranks of soldiers to present their points to the enemy at once. It was central to the conquests of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/macedonian-empire">Macedonian Empire</a> and remained the core weapon of Hellenistic armies such as that of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/seleucid-empire">Seleucid Empire</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/sarissa.jpg" alt="Sarissa" width="320" height="137" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: F. Mitchell, United States Military Academy · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Makedonische_phalanx.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>The core of Antigonid power was the Macedonian phalanx, a dense formation of infantry armed with the <b>sarissa</b>, a pike some five to six metres long, supported by peltasts, cavalry and mercenaries.</blockquote><a href="/empire/antigonid-kingdom-of-macedonia">Antigonid Kingdom of Macedonia · Military</a></li><li><blockquote>He introduced the Macedonian phalanx armed with the long <b>sarissa</b> pike, gave the infantry peltai shields, helmets, greaves and cuirasses or kotthybos stomach bands, formed the elite hypaspistai and the royal bodyguards, the somatophylakes, adopted the Scythian flying-wedge cavalry formation, hired Cretan archers and Thracian, Paeonian and Illyrian…</blockquote><a href="/empire/kingdom-of-macedon">Kingdom of Macedon · Military</a></li><li><blockquote>Philip II's phalanx carried the <b>sarissa</b>, a pike of up to about six metres, letting several ranks present their points to the enemy at once.</blockquote><a href="/empire/macedonian-empire">Macedonian Empire · At a glance</a></li><li><blockquote>The Seleucid army was built around the Macedonian-style phalanx, dense ranks of infantry armed with the <b>sarissa</b>, a pike some five to seven metres long that presented an almost impenetrable wall of points to any frontal assault, supported by Companion cavalry on the flanks, war elephants as shock…</blockquote><a href="/empire/seleucid-empire">Seleucid Empire · Military</a></li></ul></section>
